title: "SMTP connection failover"
section: "Build and configure"
description: "Use another configured Mailer when an SMTP connection fails, without replaying a message that might already have been accepted."
---
  <section>
    <div class="wide">
      <p>Your application normally sends through A. If A cannot provide a usable connection, another configured Mailer, B, can take over.
        When A recovers, new work returns to A. You keep calling the same Mailer.</p>
      <p>This is connection failover, not message retry. Once the provider starts submitting an email, Simple Java Mail does not send it again
        through another destination. A missing final SMTP reply could mean the first server already accepted it.</p>
      <p>Failover also isn't load balancing. A healthy but busy pool waits normally; it doesn't spill work to B. Use
        <a href="/smtp-connection-pooling.html">pool and cluster configuration</a> to distribute ordinary load.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
